  "explainable-ai": ["Explainable AI", "Techniques such as SHAP, LIME and feature importance that make predictions inspectable.", "Like a doctor explaining why they reached a diagnosis.", "S.L.F.C = SHAP, LIME, Feature importance, Counterfactuals", "shap.TreeExplainer(model).shap_values(X)", "Why does explainability matter in regulated sectors?", "People affected have a right to understand and contest decisions", "It improves accuracy", "It reduces training time"],
  "ai-in-industry": ["AI in Industry", "Value comes from workflow integration, data quality and change management — not model choice alone.", "Like a great engine still needing a car built around it.", "U.D.I.M = Use case, Data, Integration, Measure ROI", "Start with one measurable workflow, baseline it, then automate the narrow slice.", "What most often causes AI projects to fail?", "Poor problem framing and integration, not model accuracy", "Insufficient GPU memory", "Too much documentation"],
